LINKING EXCEPTION
=================

As a special exception, the copyright holders of Advanced Rocketry give you
permission to link or combine independent modules with Advanced Rocketry solely
through its public API — the `zmaster587.advancedRocketry.api` package and its
subpackages — to produce a combined work, and to convey the resulting combined
work under terms of your choice, provided that:

  (a) the independent module uses Advanced Rocketry only through that public
      API, and is not otherwise derived from or based on Advanced Rocketry; and

  (b) you comply with the GNU General Public License, version 3, for Advanced
      Rocketry itself and for any modifications you make to it.

An "independent module" is a module which is not derived from or based on
Advanced Rocketry other than through the public API named above. Depending on,
linking against, or calling that public API does not, by itself, make your work
a work based on Advanced Rocketry for the purposes of this License.

If you modify Advanced Rocketry itself — any code outside the public API named
above — this exception does not extend to those modifications, which remain
governed by the GNU General Public License, version 3.

You may, at your option, remove this exception from a given copy of the program;
doing so makes the plain GNU General Public License, version 3, apply to that
copy.


